IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ec59-nouns`
IMPORT `ec59-cross-references`

-- Row il-59. EXPECTED RED: eight assertions, all failing, two about each of four items. The count (8) is declared in check.sh and in encoding.json.
-- Each states what the printed words need. Nothing here is edited to make it pass.
-- Item 2: fee item (a)(3) names section 28; the consolidation prints section 28 with a repeal marker, and Sefer HaChukim 2781 p. 247 s 11 repeals it.
-- Item 3: fee item (b)(5) names an application to regulate monopoly actions under section 30; the consolidation prints section 30 as in force, and it holds no application of that kind.
-- Item 4: the notice of Kovetz HaTakanot 11002 p. 948 prints the index of November 2023 against the index of November 2021, two years apart; the notice before it prints one year apart.
-- Item 5: the 1964 regulations name section 10א of the 1959 Law as the source of the power to make them; the consolidation prints the 1959 Law as repealed (section 53).
-- Item 1, the old name in printed titles, is a record and has no assertion here.

§ `Item 2: fee item (a)(3) needs a section that is in force`

-- 1. The description of the target is the description of what the citing words point at.
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: fee item (a)(3) to section 28`)
-- 2. The consolidation prints the named section as in force.
#ASSERT `the consolidation prints the named text as in force` (`reference: fee item (a)(3) to section 28`)

§ `Item 3: fee item (b)(5) needs a section that holds the application it names`

-- 3. The description of the target is the description of what the citing words point at.
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: fee item (b)(5) to section 30`)
-- 4. The target holds a proceeding of the kind the citing words name.
#ASSERT `the target holds the kind of proceeding the citing words name` (`reference: fee item (b)(5) to section 30`)

§ `Item 4: the recital needs an earlier index of the year before the later index`

-- 5. The earlier index year is the year before the later index year.
#ASSERT `the earlier index is the one of the year before the later index` (`recital: Kovetz HaTakanot 11002, p. 948`)
-- 6. The two years are one year apart.
#ASSERT `years between the two indexes printed` (`recital: Kovetz HaTakanot 11002, p. 948`) EQUALS 1

§ `Item 5: the 1964 regulations need a power in a Law that is in force`

-- 7. The description of the target is the description of what the citing words point at.
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: the 1964 regulations' power line to section 10א of the 1959 Law`)
-- 8. The consolidation prints the named text as in force.
#ASSERT `the consolidation prints the named text as in force` (`reference: the 1964 regulations' power line to section 10א of the 1959 Law`)
